#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:4
msgid "GnuToolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/experimental_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and subject to breaking changes. See :ref:`the "
"Conan stability<stability>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:8
msgid ""
"The ``GnuToolchain`` is the toolchain generator for Autotools and other GNU-"
"like build systems. It is a more modern and usable alternative to "
"the :ref:`AutotoolsToolchain<conan_tools_gnu_autotoolstoolchain>`, based on "
"it, but with an improved user experience, like the dict-like "
"``configure_args``, ``make_args`` and ``autoreconf_args`` attributes or the "
"``extra_env`` attribute to customize the generated environment. It will "
"generate shell scripts containing environment variable definitions that the "
"autotools build system can understand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:16
msgid ""
"``GnuToolchain`` "
"and :ref:`AutotoolsToolchain<conan_tools_gnu_autotoolstoolchain>` are "
"mutually exclusive alternatives. Do not use both in the same recipe: choose "
"one or the other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:19
msgid "This generator can be used by name in conanfiles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:21
msgid "conanfile.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:21
msgid ""
"class Pkg(ConanFile):\n"
"    generators = \"GnuToolchain\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:27
msgid "conanfile.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:27
msgid ""
"[generators]\n"
"GnuToolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:33
msgid ""
"And it can also be fully instantiated in the conanfile ``generate()`` method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:35
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.tools.gnu import GnuToolchain\n"
"\n"
"class App(ConanFile):\n"
"    settings = \"os\", \"arch\", \"compiler\", \"build_type\"\n"
"\n"
"    def generate(self):\n"
"        tc = GnuToolchain(self)\n"
"        tc.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:49
msgid "Generated files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:51
msgid ""
"It will generate either the ``conangnutoolchain.sh`` or "
"``conangnutoolchain.bat`` files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:53
msgid ""
"$ conan install # there is a conanfile here, default is Release\n"
"$ source conangnutoolchain.sh\n"
"# or in Windows\n"
"$ conangnutoolchain.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:60
msgid ""
"These launchers will append information to the ``CPPFLAGS``, ``LDFLAGS``, "
"``CXXFLAGS``, ``CFLAGS`` environment variables that translate the settings "
"and options to the corresponding build flags like ``-stdlib=libstdc++``, ``-"
"std=gnu14``, architecture flags, etc. It will also append the folder where "
"the Conan generators are located to the ``PKG_CONFIG_PATH`` environment "
"variable. On Apple platforms, ``ASFLAGS`` is also set with architecture and "
"sysroot flags to ensure the assembler uses the same cross-compilation "
"settings as the C/C++ compilers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:68
msgid ""
"In a cross-building context, the environment variables ``CC_FOR_BUILD`` and "
"``CXX_FOR_BUILD`` are also set if the build profile defines the ``c`` and "
"``cpp`` values in the configuration variable "
"``tools.build:compiler_executables``. See more info in the :ref:`conf "
"section<conan_tools_gnu_gnutoolchain_conf>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:72
msgid ""
"This generator will also generate a file called ``conanbuild.conf`` "
"containing three keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:74
msgid "**configure_args**: Arguments to call the ``configure`` script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:75
msgid "**make_args**: Arguments to call the ``make`` script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:76
msgid "**autoreconf_args**: Arguments to call the ``autoreconf`` script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:78
msgid ""
"The :ref:`Autotools build helper<conan_tools_gnu_build_helper>` will use "
"that ``conanbuild.conf`` file to seamlessly call the configure and make "
"script using these precalculated arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:83
msgid "Customization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:85
msgid ""
"You can change some attributes before calling the ``generate()`` method if "
"you want to change some of the precalculated values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:88
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.tools.gnu import GnuToolchain\n"
"\n"
"class App(ConanFile):\n"
"    settings = \"os\", \"arch\", \"compiler\", \"build_type\"\n"
"\n"
"    def generate(self):\n"
"        tc = GnuToolchain(self)\n"
"        tc.configure_args[\"--my_argument\"] = None\n"
"        tc.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:102
msgid "The constructor of ``GnuToolchain`` accepts the following arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:104
msgid ""
"**namespace** (Defaulted to ``None``): Avoids collisions when there are "
"multiple toolchain calls in the same recipe. When set, the generated file "
"will be named *<namespace>_conanbuild.conf* instead of *conanbuild.conf*. "
"The same value must be passed to the constructor of the :ref:`Autotools "
"build helper<conan_tools_gnu_build_helper>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:107
msgid ""
"**prefix** (Defaulted to ``\"/\"``): Folder to use for the ``--prefix`` "
"argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:109
msgid "These are the attributes that can be customized:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:111
msgid ""
"**configure_args**: Dict-like object with the arguments to be passed to the "
"configure script. The keys are the argument names and the values their "
"values, or ``None`` for arguments without value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:114
msgid "By default the following arguments are passed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:116
msgid ""
"``--prefix``: Takes the ``prefix`` constructor argument, ``/`` as default "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:117
msgid "``--bindir=${prefix}/bin``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:118
msgid "``--sbindir=${prefix}/bin``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:119
msgid "``--libdir=${prefix}/lib``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:120
msgid "``--includedir=${prefix}/include``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:121
msgid "``--oldincludedir=${prefix}/include``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:122
msgid "``--datarootdir=${prefix}/res``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:124
msgid ""
"Also, depending on the ``package_type`` of the recipe, it will add by "
"default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:126
msgid ""
"``--enable-shared``, ``--disable-static`` if ``package_type`` is ``shared-"
"library``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:127
msgid ""
"``--disable-shared``, ``--enable-static`` if ``package_type`` is ``static-"
"library``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:129
msgid ""
"When cross-building, ``--host`` and ``--build`` are added with the "
"calculated GNU triplets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:131
msgid ""
"**make_args** (Defaulted to ``{}``): Dict-like object with the additional "
"arguments to be passed to the make script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:132
msgid ""
"**autoreconf_args** (Defaulted to ``{\"--force\": None, \"--install\": None}"
"``): Dict-like object with the additional arguments to be passed to the "
"autoreconf script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:134
msgid "**extra_defines** (Defaulted to ``[]``): Additional defines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:135
msgid "**extra_cxxflags** (Defaulted to ``[]``): Additional cxxflags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:136
msgid "**extra_cflags** (Defaulted to ``[]``): Additional cflags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:137
msgid "**extra_ldflags** (Defaulted to ``[]``): Additional ldflags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:138
msgid ""
"**extra_env**: :ref:`Environment<conan_tools_env_environment_model>` object "
"with the extra environment variables to define in the generated script. It "
"is initialized with some default values (like the ``CC``, ``CXX``, ``LD``, "
"``AR``, ``NM``, ``OBJDUMP``, ``RANLIB`` and ``STRIP`` variables for MSVC, "
"the Android NDK ones if ``tools.android:ndk_path`` is defined, or the ones "
"defined with ``tools.build:compiler_executables``) and the values defined "
"here have precedence over the ones calculated by the toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:143
msgid ""
"**ndebug**: \"NDEBUG\" if the ``settings.build_type`` is ``Release``, "
"``RelWithDebInfo`` or ``MinSizeRel``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:144
msgid "**gcc_cxx11_abi**: \"_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI\" if ``gcc/libstdc++``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:145
msgid "**libcxx**: Flag calculated from ``settings.compiler.libcxx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:146
msgid "**fpic**: True/False from ``options.fPIC`` if defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:147
msgid "**cppstd**: Flag from ``settings.compiler.cppstd``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:148
msgid "**arch_flag**: Flag from ``settings.arch``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:149
msgid "**arch_ld_flag**: Linker flag from ``settings.arch``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:150
msgid ""
"**threads_flags**: List of flags to enable threads, if applicable for the "
"compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:151
msgid "**build_type_flags**: Flags from ``settings.build_type``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:152
msgid "**build_type_link_flags**: Linker flags from ``settings.build_type``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:153
msgid "**sysroot_flag**: To pass the ``--sysroot`` flag to the compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:154
msgid ""
"**apple_arch_flag**: Only when cross-building with Apple systems. Flags from "
"``settings.arch``. For universal binaries, contains multiple ``-arch`` flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:155
msgid ""
"**apple_isysroot_flag**: Only when cross-building with Apple systems. Path "
"to the root sdk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:156
msgid ""
"**apple_min_version_flag**: Only for Apple systems, defines the ``-"
"m{ios,macosx,watchos,tvos,...}-version-min=xxx`` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:157
msgid ""
"**msvc_runtime_flag**: Flag from ``settings.compiler.runtime_type`` when "
"compiler is ``msvc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:158
msgid ""
"**msvc_extra_flags**: Extra flags for MSVC (like ``-FS``) that are "
"automatically added to the ``CXXFLAGS`` and ``CFLAGS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:159
msgid ""
"**msvc_runtime_link_flags**: Extra linker flags when using ``clang`` with "
"the MSVC runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:160
msgid ""
"**asflags**: List of assembler flags set in the ``ASFLAGS`` environment "
"variable. On Apple platforms, populated with ``arch_flag``, "
"``sysroot_flag``, ``apple_isysroot_flag``, ``apple_arch_flag``, and "
"``apple_min_version_flag``. Empty on non-Apple platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/gnu/gnutoolchain.rst:165
